# Day 19/50 — Network Protocols

Imagine two people trying to have a conversation, but neither understands the other's language.
The connection exists, but communication doesn't really happen.

Computers face a similar problem.

That's why networks use **protocols** — a set of rules that define how devices communicate and exchange data.

HTTP helps transfer web content
TCP provides reliable data delivery
IP helps route packets across networks.

Different protocols have different responsibilities, but together they make communication possible

A connection alone doesn't guarantee understanding, there has to be a common set of rules

**Because communication isn't just about sending something. It's about making sure the other side can receive and understand it.**
